    "body": "## Motivation\n\n#44747 changed `docker/Dockerfile`'s Dynamo step: a stable `ai-dynamo` pin, the frozen constraints, `inflect`, a `grpcio-tools` pin and `INSTALL_DYNAMO`. This stack leaves `docker/Dockerfile` unchanged and carried equivalent pins in the Beam image (#45253). They now live here so they can be dropped without touching the image layer.\n\nThis PR's base branch is `beam-stack-01-docker`, so its diff shows only the pins.\n\n## Modifications\n\nOn top of #45253's `docker/beam/beam.Dockerfile`:\n- Pins `grpcio-tools==1.84.0` alongside the OpenAI and tileiras pins.\n- Adds an `INSTALL_DYNAMO=1` step that installs `ai-dynamo==1.5.1` and `inflect` under the frozen constraints, releases only the pydantic pins for that solve, and records the versions it selects. `INSTALL_DYNAMO=0` skips it.\n\n## Validation\n\nBeam serving does not need these pins:\n- An image built from the unchanged upstream `docker/Dockerfile` (arm64, CUDA 13.0.3) serves Beam on 4×GB300: GSM8K 96.36% with zero request errors. It used the cuBLAS router, since that image has no `tileiras`.\n- In that image the unbounded Dynamo install resolved to `ai-dynamo==1.6.0.dev20261019`, not the empty placeholder, and `import dynamo.runtime, inflect` works. `grpcio-tools` resolved to 1.84.0 without a pin.\n- `pip check` there does report the two conflicts these pins avoid: `inflect` 7.5.0 needs `typeguard>=4` (2.13.3 installed), and `ai-dynamo-runtime` needs `pydantic<=2.13.5` (2.14.1 installed).\n- `docker buildx build --check` passes for this file; the image has not been built.\n\nThis PR is likely to be closed without merging.\n\n## Merge order\n\nEvery part targets `main`. #44747 stays open, unchanged, as the full reference. Merge in this order:\n\n1. #45253 — Beam CUDA Docker image\n2. #45291 — OpenAI SDK 2.8.0, needed by the Responses shell tools in #45257\n3. #45254 — Kernels\n4. #45255 — Attention, memory and DFlash DP support\n5. #45256 — Beam model, checkpoints and tests\n6. #45257 — Beam reasoning, tool calls and response templates (also after #40478, #43941 and #40479)\n7. #45290 — `nvidia-cuda-tileiras`, needed by #45361\n8. #45361 — cuTile BF16x3 router GEMM (optional: without it Beam uses the cuBLAS router)\n\nThis PR is not in the merge order for now.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39360922456](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39360922456)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39360922755](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39360922755)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
